## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/task/subagent_tools.dart | ⚠️ important network peer name resolution shadows local identities in agent message resolvefabricaddress now resolves network dm peers before every local identity lib src task subagent tools dart 1026 1031 dart final networktarget networkerror resolvenetworkdmpeeraddress manager to if networkerror null return to networkerror if networktarget null return networktarget null only after this selfid main local handles child names fabric directory resolvenetworkdmpeeraddress matches a peer by exact id safe — network dm n is synthetic but then by exact display name peer names come from the remote side — the dm envelope fromname roster label agent cli inbox dart 123 agent cli network dart 49 — so a remote peer can label itself main or the display name of an existing local sibling or fabric session when that happens agent message to main the documented parent keyword or a name addressed steer that used to reach the local mailbox is silently delivered to the remote peer over the encrypted transport — no error no ambiguity prompt the fail closed ambiguity check covers network vs network duplicates only test task subagent tools test dart asserts peer id duplicate id not network vs local collisions suggested fix keep the alias win close the shadow dart 1 exact network peer id synthetic namespace — keep as is 2 resolve local identities first selfid local handles child names fabric directory names 3 fall through to network peer name match only when no local identity claimed the string — or include the matched local identity in the ambiguity error so the model picks an id repro sketch register a peer named main or a name equal to a child handle then call agent message to main — it routes to the peer address instead of manager selfid a test asserting to main still reaches the parent and that a peer named like a local sibling fails closed with usable ids would pin the contract |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

